n          \"encounterId\": \"enc-new\",\n          \"definitionId\": \"animal-001\",\n          \"location\": {\n            \"source\": \"manual\",\n            \"description\": \"Synthetic park, north path\"\n          },\n          \"photoRef\": \"photo-a\",\n          \"nickname\": \"Reed\"\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has no encounters and collection storage fails before the write commits\n      When the animal encounter is recorded for the authenticated user\n      Then the individual animal is recorded once for this request or a named refusal leaves the collection unchanged\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.reason.code | COLLECTION_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.mutation.applied | false |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter | (absent) |\n\n  Rule: Retries of one request do not collapse distinct encounters or duplicate the same encounter\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E05, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D07.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-encounter-retry.json (sha256:23a0e4362e64bcd63c81eaaa5d7b2f12128f1f2e442544a8790d07f093124d75).\n    @case:nrd-encounter-retry\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Retrying the same request returns its one existing encounter\n      Given an encounter request with an animal selection, location, photo reference and optional nickname\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"encounterId\": \"enc-new\",\n          \"definitionId\": \"animal-001\",\n          \"location\": {\n            \"source\": \"manual\",\n            \"description\": \"Synthetic park, north path\"\n          },\n          \"photoRef\": \"photo-a\",\n          \"nickname\": \"Reed\"\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery''s identical request for enc-new was already committed\n      When the animal encounter is recorded for the authenticated user\n      Then the individual animal is recorded once for this request or a named refusal leaves the collection unchanged\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.status | RECORDED |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.encounterId | enc-new |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.mutation.applied | false |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.replayed | true |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.photoRef | photo-a |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.nickname | Reed |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.ownerUserId | user-a |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E05, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D07.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-encounter-id-conflict.json (sha256:f9e13f1bf0179048d019ebca724e03130bd16458092a1b8d2aa0733f9f260577).\n    @case:nrd-encounter-id-conflict\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Reusing the request identity with changed content is refused\n      Given an encounter request with an animal selection, location, photo reference and optional nickname\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"encounterId\": \"enc-new\",\n          \"definitionId\": \"animal-001\",\n          \"location\": {\n            \"source\": \"manual\",\n            \"description\": \"Synthetic park, north path\"\n          },\n          \"photoRef\": \"photo-a\",\n          \"nickname\": \"Changed\"\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery''s enc-new was already committed with the nickname Reed\n      When the animal encounter is recorded for the authenticated user\n      Then the individual animal is recorded once for this request or a named refusal leaves the collection unchanged\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.reason.code | ENCOUNTER_ID_CONFLICT |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.mutation.applied | false |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter | (absent) |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U02, NRD-E05, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D07.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-encounter-same-id-other-owner.json (sha256:65d827682b3d15ce1a6cc8a92ef584bfb19e238a4a83676d83d591ccba573d5b).\n    @case:nrd-encounter-same-id-other-owner\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A second user can record a personal encounter with the same request ID\n      Given an encounter request with an animal selection, location, photo reference and optional nickname\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"encounterId\": \"enc-new\",\n          \"definitionId\": \"animal-001\",\n          \"location\": {\n            \"source\": \"manual\",\n            \"description\": \"Synthetic park, north path\"\n          },\n          \"photoRef\": \"photo-other\",\n          \"nickname\": \"Brook\"\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has already committed enc-new and Blake is signed in with Blake''s own photo\n      When the animal encounter is recorded for the authenticated user\n      Then the individual animal is recorded once for this request or a named refusal leaves the collection unchanged\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.status | RECORDED |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.encounterId | enc-new |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.ownerUserId | user-b |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.photoRef | photo-other |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.encounter.nickname | Brook |\n        | nerdery-record-animal-encounter.record | $.mutation.applied | true |\n"}';
INSERT @minted(value) EXEC model.mint_content_artifact @document=N'{"artifactKind":"capability-feature:nerdery-view-collected-animals","text":"# nerdery-view-collected-animals: canonical-feature candidate for owner review, 2026-11-02.\n# Product authority: source/nerdery-architecture-design-challenge.pdf, identified in source/source-manifest.json.\n# Authoring convention: the two supplied canonical feature examples; not a new platform format.\n# Status: finalized for the SideFX build of the citizen slice from the owner-review candidate\n# nerdery-canonical-features/features/mvp/nerdery-view-collected-animals.feature (sha256:7367cc04657b8ecdfa401520b649ab79117ab88b9035ec232c2fcabe00072ee4).\n# @status:probed: the case ran read-only against the wildlife procedures through nerdery/conformance/run-cases.mjs\n# (runs 84ff8efb, c901e190, 8e66151b, 7837a8f1, b28d02da, 25e64090).\n# Every Scenario below is an acceptance case of the ONE circuit scenario tagged on this Feature.\n# Given / When / Then are exact across cases. Given holds the request JSON. Then holds operation/path/equals.\n# Values: true/false/null/numbers/arrays/objects are JSON values; other values are strings; (absent) selects nothing.\n# Authentication, fixture state and dependency behavior come from the pinned test arrangement, never caller role claims.\n# Provider: the operation is one sql-database-reader statement on sfx-identity (EXEC wildlife.serve), so every case is\n# tagged @provider:sql-database-reader.\n# The JSON under Given is the request body. The declared API operation binds the caller from the session the frontdoor\n# validated; the capability input is {caller, request}. Fixture preparation is separate.\n# A successful write requires durable provider testimony and independent read-back; output echoes are not proof.\n# All JSON shapes/identities are proposed under D01. Case design decisions remain proposals, not Nerdery requirements.\n# Scope: mvp. Source requirements: NRD-U03, NRD-E05, NRD-E06, NRD-E07.\n# Proposed outcome contract: nerdery-view-collected-animals-result.v1; terminal variants: LISTED, REFUSED.\n# Proposed operation identity: nerdery-view-collected-animals.view.\n\n@capability:nerdery-view-collected-animals\n@root-scenario:nerdery-view-collected-animals\n@scenario:nerdery-view-collected-animals\n@input:nerdery-view-collected-animals-request\n@input-contract:nerdery-view-collected-animals-request.v1\n@event:nerdery-view-collected-animals-requested\n@event-authority:nerdery-view-collected-animals.v1\n@outcome:nerdery-view-collected-animals-outcome\n@outcome-contract:nerdery-view-collected-animals-result.v1\n@outcome-terminal\nFeature: View the individual animals in a personal collection\n  As a citizen or biologist\n  I want to view the individual animals I recorded\n  So that I recognize my animals by my photos and optional nicknames\n\n  Rule: Repeated encounters remain separate individuals and use the user''s photo and nickname\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E05, NRD-E06, NRD-E07.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D14.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-individuals.json (sha256:858370102cf37aeb9eea7abb646f188c66a8cfa9e0789f3aa75ea2c0cfb51075).\n    # Fixture encounter order is explicit; the product''s general collected-list sorting policy is not prescribed by the brief.\n    @case:nrd-collected-individuals\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Two encounters of one definition remain two individual collection entries\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has two distinct encounters with Demo Heron, with different photos and nicknames\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | LISTED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.total | 2 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].encounterId | enc-001 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[1].encounterId | enc-002 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].definitionId | animal-001 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[1].definitionId | animal-001 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].photoRef | photo-a |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[1].photoRef | photo-b |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].displayName | Reed |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[1].displayName | Sky |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[2] | (absent) |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E06, NRD-E07.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-fallback-name.json (sha256:6175e14f973f8a7c83838dc2732efb528c73fd6c8c64c86478a1c203253a7e80).\n    @case:nrd-collected-fallback-name\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Without a nickname the common name labels the user''s photo\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery''s only encounter is a Demo Fox with a personal photo and no nickname\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | LISTED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.total | 1 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].displayName | Demo Fox |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].photoRef | photo-a |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].nickname | null |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-empty.json (sha256:51867b50c235cf1ec4648f7c50723336f16c2284ddd39852c525a9946ad7f53e).\n    @case:nrd-collected-empty\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A user without encounters has an empty personal collection\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery is signed in and the collection has no encounters\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | LISTED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.total | 0 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items | [] |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-ownership.json (sha256:7385b038f7c2db9b4d8196095023e372d580fced382430bb5d3e5afdcf1770cc).\n    @case:nrd-collected-ownership\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The personal collection contains only the authenticated user''s individuals\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Blake owns enc-008 and all other fixture encounters belong to other users\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | LISTED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.total | 1 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].encounterId | enc-008 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].ownerUserId | user-b |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[1] | (absent) |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U03, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-biologist.json (sha256:59a3c2750da418ac22f7a7b3cdc91cb03a019b0d33be5f611716fa501997d1be).\n    @case:nrd-collected-biologist\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A biologist can view their own collected individual\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is signed in as a biologist and owns the individual enc-009\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | LISTED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.total | 1 |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items[0].encounterId | enc-009 |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-collected-anonymous.json (sha256:4fe17fb5508d2af78bacc24472df7a6d174778770bde6e113ef3e85e83343725).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-collected-anonymous\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An unauthenticated request cannot read a personal collection\n      Given a personal collected-animals request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And no authenticated subject is available for the personal collection\n      When the recorded individuals are read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user can view their individual collected animals or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.reason.code | AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED |\n        | nerdery-view-collected-animals.view | $.items | (absent) |\n"}';
INSERT @minted(value) EXEC model.mint_content_artifact @document=N'{"artifactKind":"capability-feature:nerdery-set-animal-team","text":"# nerdery-set-animal-team: canonical-feature candidate for owner review, 2026-11-02.\n# Product authority: source/nerdery-architecture-design-challenge.pdf, identified in source/source-manifest.json.\n# Authoring convention: the two supplied canonical feature examples; not a new platform format.\n# Status: finalized for the SideFX build of the citizen slice from the owner-review candidate\n# nerdery-canonical-features/features/mvp/nerdery-set-animal-team.feature (sha256:f7dab2b2f441f1501f074730a2e6981ef8345e1ac181d3d6a77d4a770f7fa13a).\n# @status:probed: the case ran read-only against the wildlife procedures through nerdery/conformance/run-cases.mjs\n# (runs 84ff8efb, c901e190, 8e66151b, 7837a8f1, b28d02da, 25e64090).\n# Every Scenario below is an acceptance case of the ONE circuit scenario tagged on this Feature.\n# Given / When / Then are exact across cases. Given holds the request JSON. Then holds operation/path/equals.\n# Values: true/false/null/numbers/arrays/objects are JSON values; other values are strings; (absent) selects nothing.\n# Authentication, fixture state and dependency behavior come from the pinned test arrangement, never caller role claims.\n# Provider: the operation is one sql-database-reader statement on sfx-identity (EXEC wildlife.serve), so every case is\n# tagged @provider:sql-database-reader.\n# The JSON under Given is the request body. The declared API operation binds the caller from the session the frontdoor\n# validated; the capability input is {caller, request}. Fixture preparation is separate.\n# A successful write requires durable provider testimony and independent read-back; output echoes are not proof.\n# All JSON shapes/identities are proposed under D01. Case design decisions remain proposals, not Nerdery requirements.\n# Scope: mvp. Source requirements: NRD-U02, NRD-U03, NRD-E05, NRD-E06, NRD-T01.\n# Proposed outcome contract: nerdery-set-animal-team-result.v1; terminal variants: SAVED, REFUSED.\n# Proposed operation identity: nerdery-set-animal-team.set.\n\n@capability:nerdery-set-animal-team\n@root-scenario:nerdery-set-animal-team\n@scenario:nerdery-set-animal-team\n@input:nerdery-set-animal-team-request\n@input-contract:nerdery-set-animal-team-request.v1\n@event:nerdery-set-animal-team-requested\n@event-authority:nerdery-set-animal-team.v1\n@outcome:nerdery-set-animal-team-outcome\n@outcome-contract:nerdery-set-animal-team-result.v1\n@outcome-terminal\nFeature: Select a personal team of up to six collected animals\n  As a citizen or biologist\n  I want to select my team from my collected individuals\n  So that my chosen animals can appear together on my home page\n\n  Rule: A team has at most six distinct owned collected individuals and is replaced atomically\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U02, NRD-T01, NRD-E05, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-two-individuals.json (sha256:1c94f883fdf3ded4cdc2f52ac6a913efcba2312acbe0baed11d4cd72bfa23182).\n    @case:nrd-team-two-individuals\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Two individuals of the same definition may both be selected\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And enc-001 and enc-002 are two of Avery''s recorded individuals of the same animal definition\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | SAVED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.encounterIds | [\"enc-001\",\"enc-002\"] |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.size | 2 |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.revision | 2 |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-six.json (sha256:61f3cb8960c8de8f9e1cadcf764ba8321a3716e85003e3dde65c3480a8fa5479).\n    @case:nrd-team-six\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Exactly six collected individuals is permitted\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\",\n            \"enc-003\",\n            \"enc-004\",\n            \"enc-005\",\n            \"enc-006\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery owns all seven candidate individuals and the current team is at revision 1\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | SAVED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.encounterIds | [\"enc-001\",\"enc-002\",\"enc-003\",\"enc-004\",\"enc-005\",\"enc-006\"] |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.size | 6 |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-clear.json (sha256:167fd0005b67993dfc59bdbc5666a33f0de93ff32eeb63fdfbc0fc49fc94baa5).\n    @case:nrd-team-clear\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An empty selection clears the team\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": []\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has two saved team members and submits an empty selection\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | SAVED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.encounterIds | [] |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.size | 0 |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-seven.json (sha256:c4f475785995550e8ed45cdfda5064c5e066244e664751c247db46e49feba3c4).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-team-seven\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A seventh individual cannot be added\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\",\n            \"enc-003\",\n            \"enc-004\",\n            \"enc-005\",\n            \"enc-006\",\n            \"enc-007\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery owns all seven candidate individuals and the current team is at revision 1\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | TEAM_LIMIT_EXCEEDED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n  Rule: A team can contain only distinct individuals the user has recorded\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-uncollected.json (sha256:b5ea629e1d288f50277c08f7bcbb59c097f0c9a2bfaec1df33c4b490969489c0).\n    @case:nrd-team-uncollected\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An unrecorded animal cannot occupy a team slot\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-missing\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And no encounter exists at enc-missing\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | TEAM_MEMBER_NOT_AVAILABLE |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01, NRD-E06.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-foreign.json (sha256:6aab996c644f81cbead4ed0bd39073fd25815195e254fbc2c45fb927ea4c8f3e).\n    @case:nrd-team-foreign\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Another user''s individual cannot occupy a team slot\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-008\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And enc-008 belongs to Blake and Avery is selecting the team\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | TEAM_MEMBER_NOT_AVAILABLE |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-duplicate.json (sha256:90015ddfe740358c9c8d5ca15a7305a35e541830ed0b66fb96fc6e0afde94716).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-team-duplicate\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The same encounter cannot occupy two team slots\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-001\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And the same encounter ID occurs twice in Avery''s request\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | TEAM_MEMBER_DUPLICATE |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n  Rule: A refused replacement preserves the saved team\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-stale.json (sha256:0c4af54fa69bbf5044ff1feaeea63512eab78c43911333347f848c4b572b2450).\n    @case:nrd-team-stale\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A stale team edit preserves the newer selection\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 0,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery''s saved team has revision 1 and the submitted revision is stale\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | REVISION_CONFLICT |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U03, NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-biologist.json (sha256:6a0d848c7254da6229e44e3163629817f0fe2a2bfc1c502d592856e98d9cdd93).\n    @case:nrd-team-biologist\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A biologist can select a personal team\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-009\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is signed in as a biologist and owns enc-009\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | SAVED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.ownerUserId | user-bio |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.team.encounterIds | [\"enc-009\"] |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-anonymous.json (sha256:5279976c6a1e937f2ddd3b63e24eb3a5b6e3f5453442a28752fd0c9953071b98).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-team-anonymous\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An unauthenticated caller cannot save a team\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And there is no authenticated team owner\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D06, D13.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-team-storage-failure.json (sha256:d675e76d2f0ed135c4ba0de88e68ae9ac1af5413d104a0c578c7d802226fe1ce).\n    @case:nrd-team-storage-failure\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A failed team write preserves the previous team\n      Given a proposed team of collected encounter identities\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"expectedRevision\": 1,\n          \"encounterIds\": [\n            \"enc-001\",\n            \"enc-002\"\n          ]\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery already has a saved team and storage fails before the replacement commits\n      When the team selection is saved for the authenticated user\n      Then the selected team of at most six animals is saved or a named refusal preserves the previous team\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.reason.code | TEAM_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE |\n        | nerdery-set-animal-team.set | $.mutation.applied | false |\n"}';
INSERT @minted(value) EXEC model.mint_content_artifact @document=N'{"artifactKind":"capability-feature:nerdery-view-wildlife-home","text":"# nerdery-view-wildlife-home: canonical-feature candidate for owner review, 2026-11-02.\n# Product authority: source/nerdery-architecture-design-challenge.pdf, identified in source/source-manifest.json.\n# Authoring convention: the two supplied canonical feature examples; not a new platform format.\n# Status: finalized for the SideFX build of the citizen slice from the owner-review candidate\n# nerdery-canonical-features/features/mvp/nerdery-view-wildlife-home.feature (sha256:2ef10443b9b117d2987e0050439e610796ef08743ef4dc327337ae5d9c082339).\n# @status:probed: the case ran read-only against the wildlife procedures through nerdery/conformance/run-cases.mjs\n# (runs 84ff8efb, c901e190, 8e66151b, 7837a8f1, b28d02da, 25e64090).\n# Every Scenario below is an acceptance case of the ONE circuit scenario tagged on this Feature.\n# Given / When / Then are exact across cases. Given holds the request JSON. Then holds operation/path/equals.\n# Values: true/false/null/numbers/arrays/objects are JSON values; other values are strings; (absent) selects nothing.\n# Authentication, fixture state and dependency behavior come from the pinned test arrangement, never caller role claims.\n# Provider: the operation is one sql-database-reader statement on sfx-identity (EXEC wildlife.serve), so every case is\n# tagged @provider:sql-database-reader.\n# The JSON under Given is the request body. The declared API operation binds the caller from the session the frontdoor\n# validated; the capability input is {caller, request}. Fixture preparation is separate.\n# A successful write requires durable provider testimony and independent read-back; output echoes are not proof.\n# All JSON shapes/identities are proposed under D01. Case design decisions remain proposals, not Nerdery requirements.\n# Scope: mvp. Source requirements: NRD-E07, NRD-T02.\n# Proposed outcome contract: nerdery-view-wildlife-home-result.v1; terminal variants: VISIBLE, REFUSED.\n# Proposed operation identity: nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view.\n\n@capability:nerdery-view-wildlife-home\n@root-scenario:nerdery-view-wildlife-home\n@scenario:nerdery-view-wildlife-home\n@input:nerdery-view-wildlife-home-request\n@input-contract:nerdery-view-wildlife-home-request.v1\n@event:nerdery-view-wildlife-home-requested\n@event-authority:nerdery-view-wildlife-home.v1\n@outcome:nerdery-view-wildlife-home-outcome\n@outcome-contract:nerdery-view-wildlife-home-result.v1\n@outcome-terminal\nFeature: View the selected team on the wildlife home page\n  As a signed-in user\n  I want to see my selected team on the home page\n  So that my personal wildlife team is immediately recognizable\n\n  Rule: The logged-in home page shows the saved team with individual photos and display names\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T02, NRD-E07.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06, D14.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-home-saved-team.json (sha256:30de662e05f166a048291370171bf114fd40c90c88bef1eb97ee118244c1b00c).\n    @case:nrd-home-saved-team\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The home page presents the saved individuals rather than all collected animals\n      Given a wildlife home-page request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has selected enc-001 and enc-003 in that order from a larger collection\n      When the home-page experience is read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user sees their saved team or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.status | VISIBLE |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.size | 2 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[0].encounterId | enc-001 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[0].displayName | Reed |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[0].photoRef | photo-a |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[1].encounterId | enc-003 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[1].displayName | Demo Fox |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[1].photoRef | photo-a |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[2] | (absent) |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-home-no-team.json (sha256:0dd56c24c195ed20dd7102adcb0c12a8044011150ba173dda5a91e89958e59e3).\n    @case:nrd-home-no-team\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A logged-in user without a selection sees an empty team\n      Given a wildlife home-page request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey has a collected individual but an empty saved team\n      When the home-page experience is read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user sees their saved team or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.status | VISIBLE |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.size | 0 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members | [] |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05, D06.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-home-user-specific.json (sha256:e4ddae04797d7ff228252af36866314e8dbb66a7e212bc08c8dda9e2fa2d21b5).\n    @case:nrd-home-user-specific\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The home page does not reuse another user''s saved team\n      Given a wildlife home-page request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And Blake''s team contains enc-008 and Avery''s saved team contains different individuals\n      When the home-page experience is read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user sees their saved team or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.status | VISIBLE |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.size | 1 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[0].encounterId | enc-008 |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team.members[1] | (absent) |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-T02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-home-team-anonymous.json (sha256:6aaceba8d35fa8f9c209c2a9dbadbb0055ccd4bfc986f1a380ebb93ede5763f0).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-home-team-anonymous\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An anonymous request cannot receive a private saved team\n      Given a wildlife home-page request\n        \"\"\"json\n        {}\n        \"\"\"\n      And no user is logged in\n      When the home-page experience is read for the authenticated user\n      Then the user sees their saved team or a named refusal\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.reason.code | AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED |\n        | nerdery-view-wildlife-home.view | $.team | (absent) |\n"}';
INSERT @minted(value) EXEC model.mint_content_artifact @document=N'{"artifactKind":"capability-feature:nerdery-add-animal-definition","text":"# nerdery-add-animal-definition: canonical-feature candidate for owner review, 2026-11-02.\n# Product authority: source/nerdery-architecture-design-challenge.pdf, identified in source/source-manifest.json.\n# Authoring convention: the two supplied canonical feature examples; not a new platform format.\n# Status: finalized for the SideFX build of the citizen slice from the owner-review candidate\n# nerdery-canonical-features/features/mvp/nerdery-add-animal-definition.feature (sha256:feee15f08dbad7a802741b1006ba16cba7e77dee4605b529bf40c1fa729fd89e).\n# @status:probed: the case ran read-only against the wildlife procedures through nerdery/conformance/run-cases.mjs\n# (runs 84ff8efb, c901e190, 8e66151b, 7837a8f1, b28d02da, 25e64090).\n# Every Scenario below is an acceptance case of the ONE circuit scenario tagged on this Feature.\n# Given / When / Then are exact across cases. Given holds the request JSON. Then holds operation/path/equals.\n# Values: true/false/null/numbers/arrays/objects are JSON values; other values are strings; (absent) selects nothing.\n# Authentication, fixture state and dependency behavior come from the pinned test arrangement, never caller role claims.\n# Provider: the operation is one sql-database-reader statement on sfx-identity (EXEC wildlife.serve), so every case is\n# tagged @provider:sql-database-reader.\n# The JSON under Given is the request body. The declared API operation binds the caller from the session the frontdoor\n# validated; the capability input is {caller, request}. Fixture preparation is separate.\n# A successful write requires durable provider testimony and independent read-back; output echoes are not proof.\n# All JSON shapes/identities are proposed under D01. Case design decisions remain proposals, not Nerdery requirements.\n# Scope: mvp. Source requirements: NRD-U01, NRD-D01, NRD-D02, NRD-D03, NRD-D04, NRD-D05, NRD-A01, NRD-A02.\n# Proposed outcome contract: nerdery-add-animal-definition-result.v1; terminal variants: ADDED, REFUSED.\n# Proposed operation identity: nerdery-add-animal-definition.add.\n\n@capability:nerdery-add-animal-definition\n@root-scenario:nerdery-add-animal-definition\n@scenario:nerdery-add-animal-definition\n@input:nerdery-add-animal-definition-request\n@input-contract:nerdery-add-animal-definition-request.v1\n@event:nerdery-add-animal-definition-requested\n@event-authority:nerdery-add-animal-definition.v1\n@outcome:nerdery-add-animal-definition-outcome\n@outcome-contract:nerdery-add-animal-definition-result.v1\n@outcome-terminal\nFeature: Add an animal definition\n  As a biologist\n  I want to add a supported animal definition with its properties\n  So that users can discover and collect that animal\n\n  Rule: A biologist can add a complete definition that respects the stated type limit and reference catalog\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U01, NRD-D01, NRD-D02, NRD-D03, NRD-D04, NRD-D05, NRD-A01, NRD-A02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-add.json (sha256:c6c2589f2c30b14d623dd8129d4fb31223fdbd33bd9cb5d89e42e84bc94d3ffd).\n    @case:nrd-definition-add\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A biologist adds the complete definition\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is a biologist, avatar-004 is retained and public collection number 4 is available\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | ADDED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.commonName | Demo Owl |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.scientificName | Synthetic scientific label 4 |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.avatarPhotoRef | avatar-004 |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.collectionNumber | 4 |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.range | [\"county-a\"] |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.types | [\"Flying\"] |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.stats | {\"Strength\":5,\"Size\":6,\"Speed\":7} |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.attributes | [{\"attributeId\":\"habitat\",\"valueIds\":[\"woodland\"]},{\"attributeId\":\"diet\",\"valueIds\":[\"fish\"]}] |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D04.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-zero-types.json (sha256:2c1399bc90b6255371c22eadedba30790b8c29bf92c4bb7edc2f9bf931d27caf).\n    @case:nrd-definition-zero-types\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Up to two types permits zero types\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is signed in as a biologist and the type catalog has fifteen entries\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | ADDED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.types | [] |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D04.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-two-types.json (sha256:d7d3bb0c0badf8e3d2d66e3c9a2b2192877d4fe7af9fa8bef56e8d8435069528).\n    @case:nrd-definition-two-types\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Up to two types permits two types\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\",\n              \"Aquatic\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is signed in as a biologist and the type catalog has fifteen entries\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | ADDED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.animal.types | [\"Flying\",\"Aquatic\"] |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | true |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D04.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-three-types.json (sha256:2fb53e062828aa007544a42018ae85fad6e6f8b50a8a3ef60f0566e0bad9442d).\n    @case:nrd-definition-three-types\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The new definition refuses three types\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\",\n              \"Aquatic\",\n              \"Rural\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Casey is signed in as a biologist and the type catalog has fifteen entries\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_TYPE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D04.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-unknown-type.json (sha256:4268b86a683120bc7fe38d9830c717a114c8bfb2a68a8cbd955a17d94a65fcc8).\n    @case:nrd-definition-unknown-type\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The new definition refuses unknown type\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"UnknownType\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And UnknownType is absent from the type catalog\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_TYPE_UNKNOWN |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D03.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-unknown-county.json (sha256:fe9f7f0944e198ef9630cbe4b1e64c978f4a2cb3142a77ac3ae072409e1cccd8).\n    @case:nrd-definition-unknown-county\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The new definition refuses unknown county\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-unknown\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And county-unknown is absent from the fixture state''s county catalog\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | COUNTY_UNKNOWN |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-duplicate-number.json (sha256:995165dd5d5ba8911311b260d26bbdad38bb2db65ccb6df1f16a82a59d9c791b).\n    @case:nrd-definition-duplicate-number\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The new definition refuses duplicate number\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 1,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Demo Heron already holds public collection number 1\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | COLLECTION_NUMBER_NOT_UNIQUE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-A01, NRD-A02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-unknown-attribute-value.json (sha256:099cb26e820df12357eddaba1747f1c08d45c1bedf667b2ef7f80985095682da).\n    @case:nrd-definition-unknown-attribute-value\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: The new definition refuses unknown attribute value\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"desert\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And the requested association uses a value outside the attribute''s selectable values\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ATTRIBUTE_VALUE_NOT_SELECTABLE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n  Rule: A definition includes the intrinsic properties in the challenge\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-commonname.json (sha256:4787ec6703247947c4acef971e917483f6e2dfee2276427d746ca7efd53e6562).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-commonname\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires common name\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist submits the definition with the indicated intrinsic property omitted\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-scientificname.json (sha256:bcf60509ef8fdedde19e946e1563ead8015e44ca15402162a3db45d5bf7ec36d).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-scientificname\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires scientific name\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist submits the definition with the indicated intrinsic property omitted\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-avatarphotoref.json (sha256:c5c614a0ad8b3b9ebaa2181672c3ca6386cfe05f1ca5649bb9443adc7da85279).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-avatarphotoref\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires on-file photo reference\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist submits the definition with the indicated intrinsic property omitted\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D02.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-collectionnumber.json (sha256:5315f7904538484fd1e335bbc91cbd57a6db63b7f3ce0533d478c746e96bad44).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-collectionnumber\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires public collection number\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist submits the definition without a public collection number\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D03.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-range.json (sha256:aa8aa27c0831cec361615295a7440390068a319b0a261bd4030b54748a25b1f9).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-range\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires county range\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist submits the definition without its county range\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D04.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-types.json (sha256:c2147d7b7a8328412d114774b26612cb8b92cb6b9247d891683fc0365be2d415).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-types\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires types field\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist omits the types field entirely\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-D05.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D08.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-missing-stats.json (sha256:aa277eb9f598cbc5b8b64e8b57982c1ccabac53dc004da03cfd8cee86599a025).\n    @case:nrd-definition-missing-stats\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: Adding an animal definition requires stats field\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And a biologist omits the stats field entirely\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | ANIMAL_DEFINITION_INCOMPLETE |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n  Rule: Only a biologist can add a catalog definition\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-citizen-add.json (sha256:eb1eb354375391e888fc9756c375c424a02a99bdf2d5ec143651603d5a93bff3).\n    @case:nrd-definition-citizen-add\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: A citizen cannot add an animal definition\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And Avery has only the citizen role\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | BIOLOGIST_ROLE_REQUIRED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n\n    # Source requirements: NRD-U01.\n    # Proposed decisions: D01, D05.\n    # Arrangement: nerdery-canonical-features/fixtures/cases/nrd-definition-anonymous-add.json (sha256:2f960b56a3bad0e45477852f1e379505a249aeb8d5cfe60e6119cafe993902dd).\n    # Refused inside the operation''s one provider call; the stored state is unchanged.\n    @case:nrd-definition-anonymous-add\n    @status:probed\n    @provider:sql-database-reader\n    Scenario: An unauthenticated caller cannot add an animal definition\n      Given a proposed animal definition\n        \"\"\"json\n        {\n          \"animal\": {\n            \"commonName\": \"Demo Owl\",\n            \"scientificName\": \"Synthetic scientific label 4\",\n            \"avatarPhotoRef\": \"avatar-004\",\n            \"collectionNumber\": 4,\n            \"range\": [\n              \"county-a\"\n            ],\n            \"types\": [\n              \"Flying\"\n            ],\n            \"stats\": {\n              \"Strength\": 5,\n              \"Size\": 6,\n              \"Speed\": 7\n            },\n            \"attributes\": [\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"habitat\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"woodland\"\n                ]\n              },\n              {\n                \"attributeId\": \"diet\",\n                \"valueIds\": [\n                  \"fish\"\n                ]\n              }\n            ]\n          }\n        }\n        \"\"\"\n      And no subject is signed in\n      When the animal definition is added by the authenticated user\n      Then the new animal definition is available or a named refusal explains why it was not added\n        | operation | path | equals |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.status | REFUSED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.reason.code | AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED |\n        | nerdery-add-animal-definition.add | $.mutation.applied | false |\n"}';
INSERT @minted(value) EXEC model.mint_content_artifact @document=N'{"artifactKind":"flight-promise:nerdery-citizen-slice-declare","text":"{\"contractId\":\"flight-promise.v1\",\"promiseId\":\"nerdery-citizen-slice-declare\",\"workClass\":\"owner-objective\",\"statement\":\"OV3 declares the eight capabilities of the Nerdery citizen slice feature first: each from its DSL, pinned to the retained bytes of its finalized canonical feature, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT in the same change. Each runs as one sql-database-reader statement on the wildlife store, which verifies the caller''s session.\",\"obligations\":[{\"obligationId\":\"O1\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-browse-animal-collection is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-browse-animal-collection.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:dc19f2defcd1b0dcc5beead0fe42a0976336238216422d87397ccbcfcb7588c5, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:dc19f2defcd1b0dcc5beead0fe42a0976336238216422d87397ccbcfcb7588c5\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O2\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-view-animal-definition is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-view-animal-definition.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:2b4c55fd4f28e46b17394b620ba9b9d78f854557b4c85a909989023a036472c5, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:2b4c55fd4f28e46b17394b620ba9b9d78f854557b4c85a909989023a036472c5\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O3\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-upload-encounter-photo is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-upload-encounter-photo.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:38e58430acc3a39e88078f4a71000dacb3d585124a7a0cef2f906bcb35716de5, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:38e58430acc3a39e88078f4a71000dacb3d585124a7a0cef2f906bcb35716de5\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O4\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-record-animal-encounter is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-record-animal-encounter.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:df6cea9ceb5ce4d6a63755f8c42e80bc285191fecc18598e695ab6bd73e03a23, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:df6cea9ceb5ce4d6a63755f8c42e80bc285191fecc18598e695ab6bd73e03a23\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O5\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-view-collected-animals is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-view-collected-animals.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:a8f1920e6569b46ab5924fe841bebd5cc63a0993accb26f5a2e78cd20bcd835c, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:a8f1920e6569b46ab5924fe841bebd5cc63a0993accb26f5a2e78cd20bcd835c\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O6\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-set-animal-team is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-set-animal-team.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:6dd6c439568c45a7b63b8ad2745ac200f73c3d6d45e043d06b858cf0926048d2, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:6dd6c439568c45a7b63b8ad2745ac200f73c3d6d45e043d06b858cf0926048d2\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O7\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-view-wildlife-home is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-view-wildlife-home.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:d91ded8a312cb3eca7c69a6004026db720227bfb8582623674705d6dfe7e4bc4, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:d91ded8a312cb3eca7c69a6004026db720227bfb8582623674705d6dfe7e4bc4\"},{\"obligationId\":\"O8\",\"statement\":\"nerdery-add-animal-definition is declared from nerdery/dsl/nerdery-add-animal-definition.dsl, pinned to its canonical feature sha256:cecfea79150494650b84f119ec59e26c742c7bc3822601f831aaf17ee1b2c4f2, bound to those bytes and found CONFORMANT.\",\"evidence\":\"apply-declared-change COMMITTED; read-declared-capability-document $.document.feature.digest sha256:cecfea79150494650b84f119ec59e26c742c7bc3822601f831aaf17ee1b2c4f2\"}]}"}';
SELECT N'minted' AS result_set,ordinal,JSON_VALUE(value,'$.artifact_kind') AS artifact_kind,JSON_VALUE(value,'$.action') AS action,JSON_VALUE(value,'$.content_digest') AS content_digest FROM @minted ORDER BY ordinal;
DECLARE @want TABLE(ordinal int PRIMARY KEY,artifact_kind nvarchar(80),digest varchar(80));
INSERT @want VALUES(1,N'capability-feature:nerdery-browse-animal-collection','sha256:dc19f2defcd1b0dcc5beead0fe42a0976336238216422d87397ccbcfcb7588c5'),(2,N'capability-feature:nerdery-view-animal-definition','sha256:2b4c55fd4f28e46b17394b620ba9b9d78f854557b4c85a909989023a036472c5'),(3,N'capability-feature:nerdery-upload-encounter-photo','sha256:38e58430acc3a39e88078f4a71000dacb3d585124a7a0cef2f906bcb35716de5'),(4,N'capability-feature:nerdery-record-animal-encounter','sha256:df6cea9ceb5ce4d6a63755f8c42e80bc285191fecc18598e695ab6bd73e03a23'),(5,N'capability-feature:nerdery-view-collected-animals','sha256:a8f1920e6569b46ab5924fe841bebd5cc63a0993accb26f5a2e78cd20bcd835c'),(6,N'capability-feature:nerdery-set-animal-team','sha256:6dd6c439568c45a7b63b8ad2745ac200f73c3d6d45e043d06b858cf0926048d2'),(7,N'capability-feature:nerdery-view-wildlife-home','sha256:d91ded8a312cb3eca7c69a6004026db720227bfb8582623674705d6dfe7e4bc4'),(8,N'capability-feature:nerdery-add-animal-definition','sha256:cecfea79150494650b84f119ec59e26c742c7bc3822601f831aaf17ee1b2c4f2'),(9,N'flight-promise:nerdery-citizen-slice-declare','sha256:5b1e01127b38c9b63780b2d62e584ed03d162cb78f813cc6963c75d0eac2afef');
SELECT N'readback' AS result_set,w.ordinal,w.artifact_kind,w.digest,CASE WHEN EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM model.content_artifact a WHERE a.artifact_kind=w.artifact_kind COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 AND a.content_digest=CONVERT(binary(32),SUBSTRING(w.digest,8,64),2)) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END AS retained FROM @want w ORDER BY w.ordinal;
IF EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM @want w WHERE NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM model.content_artifact a WHERE a.artifact_kind=w.artifact_kind COLLATE Latin1_General_100_BIN2 AND a.content_digest=CONVERT(binary(32),SUBSTRING(w.digest,8,64),2)))
BEGIN
 RAISERROR(N'NRD02_VERIFY_FAILED: a retained text is not under the digest of its reviewed bytes; nothing is kept.',16,1);
 ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;
 SET NOEXEC ON;
END
COMMIT TRANSACTION;
GO
SET NOEXEC OFF;
